  "body": "Stacked on #3992 (which is stacked on #3990). This branch starts from `issue/1120-handle-inks`. Its own commits are 114f7b171 (the change) and eef05252f (the alpha fix of the review). e49b5a20f merges the #3990 and #3992 review fixes into this branch. Review those commits only. Merge #3990 and #3992 first.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe second family of #1120: the view cube, marker and axis inks.\n\n- Twelve colour tokens join `Tokens`. Each is also a theme-file key (`colors.<name>`):\n  - the view cube and its nav buttons: `cube_edge`, `cube_label`, `cube_glyph_on`, `cube_glyph_off`;\n  - the corner hint: `viewport_hint`;\n  - the playback tool marker: `marker_stem`, `marker_ring`, `marker_dot`;\n  - the axis triad of the Axes button and the handles: `axis_x`, `axis_y`, `axis_z`;\n  - the hover gold of the view cube dot and of the machined facet: `viewport_hover`.\n- The dark table holds the old dark-ground set of `ground_ink::cube_ink`. The light table holds the old light-ground set. No pixel changes.\n- `ground_ink::cube_ink_on(&Tokens, light)` builds the `CubeInk` from a token table. `cube_ink(light)` keeps its signature and reads the built-in table of that ground. The face and button greys stay numbers chosen by the ground.\n- `viewcube.rs` and `shell.rs` read `viewport_hover` for the gold.\n- The ground rule in `theme_files/overlay.rs`: before this change the cube chose its set by the viewport ground, not by the base. When a theme file makes the ground light on the dark base (or dark on the light base), each of the twelve keys that the file omits takes the value of the built-in table of that ground. A key that the file sets always wins. `docs/user-guide/themes.md` says so.\n- The built-in tables write `from_rgba_premultiplied(a, a, a, a)` for the old `from_white_alpha(a)`, because `from_white_alpha` is not `const`. The values are equal (ecolor 0.36.2); the test pins them against `from_white_alpha`.\n- The facet veil is `ground_ink::facet_veil(viewport_hover)`. It reads the token unmultiplied, then sets alpha 90. Thus a semi-transparent `viewport_hover` in a theme file keeps its colour (review of this PR: `#FF000080` gave `[45, 0, 0, 90]`, now `[90, 0, 0, 90]`). The built-in gold is opaque and gives the same veil as before.\n- The colour-literal guard loses the rows of `ground_ink.rs` and `viewcube.rs`. `shell.rs` goes from 9 to 7. `theme/tables.rs` goes from 38 to 62.\n- The example theme and the colour table of the user guide have the twelve keys.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1120-ground-inks.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nIn `crates/ui/tests/theme_files/viewport_inks.rs`, a module of the existing `theme_files` test binary (#3187: no new binary):\n\n- `the_built_in_columns_keep_the_view_cube_and_marker_colours`: each table carries the old literals of its ground.\n- `the_view_cube_inks_follow_the_viewport_ground_of_a_theme_file`: the ground rule, in the two directions, with a key that the file sets. This test fails when the rule is removed (checked locally).\n- `each_view_cube_ink_is_a_theme_key`: each key sets its own ink.\n- `the_facet_veil_keeps_the_hover_colour_of_a_semi_transparent_token`: the built-in gold gives the old veil, and the review probe `#FF000080` gives `[90, 0, 0, 90]`. With the old channel read it fails with `[45, 0, 0, 90]` (checked locally).\n\nAlso: `theme_example::example_loads_and_holds_the_dark_defaults` (the example equals `Tokens::DARK`), the existing `viewport_ground_tests` (cube greys and 3:1 contrast on the light ground), and `theme_files::colour_literals::no_colour_literal_outside_the_allowed_rows`.\n\n## Gates\n\nOn the head eef05252f:\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 10 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (3.1 min). It includes `ui suites: lib` and `ui suites: theme_files` (28 tests).\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps --all-targets -p camcraft-ui -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: the diff reaches none (0 steps reached).\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe same scenes as #3992: Move mode on the demo Block (move arrows, turn rings, axis balls, view cube) and two picked points, in the dark and light theme. The images come from the off-screen renderer (`egui_kittest` with the headless wgpu device, as in `guide_images`), on the demo Block at 1280 x 720. The images are on the images-only `pr-screenshots` branch of the fork, not on this branch.\n\nThe before images are the after images of #3992 (c8103e462). Each pair is identical: a pixel comparison gives 0 different pixels, in the two themes.\n\n| | Before (c8103e462) | After (eef05252f) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Handles, dark | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/3992/after-handles-dark.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/3993/after-handles-dark.png) |\n| Handles, light | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/3992/after-handles-light.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/3993/after-handles-light.png) |\n| Picks, dark | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/3992/after-picks-dark.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/3993/after-picks-dark.png) |\n| Picks, light | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/3992/after-picks-light.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/3993/after-picks-light.png) |\n\nThese images do not show the playback marker or the hover gold (the view cube dot and the machined facet show only under the pointer). The tests pin those values. The images of #3987 show the playback marker in the dark theme.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No check by hand in the GUI. The tests and the pixel comparison pin the values.\n- `shell.rs` has CRLF line ends. The commit keeps them; the diff of that file is two lines.\n\nChangelog: Themes can set the view cube, nav button, corner hint, playback marker, axis and viewport hover colours. A theme that makes the 3D view light or dark gets the matching built-in set for each colour that it omits.\n\nRefs #1120\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
